{"message":"The source states: “as of dec. 31, 2006 and 2005, the reserve for product warranties was $10 million and $4 million, respectively.” Thus 2006 reserve = 10 and 2005 reserve = 4, in millions. The change is 2006 minus 2005: 10 - 4 = 6, meaning a $6 million increase.","tool":"calculate","arguments":{"expression":"reserve_2006 - reserve_2005","variables":{"reserve_2006":{"value":10,"source":"source:q11n3","unit":"millions"},"reserve_2005":{"value":4,"source":"source:q11n4","unit":"millions"}},"sources":{"reserve_2006":"source:q11n3","reserve_2005":"source:q11n4"}}}